[al:新概念英语第四册]
[ti:46. Urban Growth]
[00:00.580]Passage 46. | 第46段。
[00:02.525]After millennia of growth so slow that each generation hardly noticed it, | 经过数千年的缓慢增长，以至于每一代人几乎都没有注意到，
[00:07.815]the cities are suddenly racing off in every direction. | 城市突然间向四面八方迅速发展。
[00:11.515]The world population goes up by 2% a year. | 世界人口每年增长2%。
[00:15.380]City population goes up by 4% a year, | 城市人口每年增长4%，
[00:18.555] but in big cities the rate may be as much as 5 and 6% a year. | 但在大城市，这一比例可能高达每年5%到6%。
[00:23.525]To give only one example of almost visible acceleration, | 仅举一个几乎可见的加速例子，
[00:28.110] Athens today grows by three dwellings and 100 square meters of road every hour. | 今天的雅典每小时增加三处住宅和100平方米的道路。
[00:33.745]There is no reason to believe that this pace will slacken. | 没有理由相信这种速度会减缓。
[00:37.520]As technology gradually swallows up all forms of work, | 随着科技逐渐吞噬所有形式的工作，
[00:41.585]industrial and agricultural, | 无论是工业的还是农业的，
[00:43.560]the rural areas are going to shrink, | 农村地区将会萎缩，
[00:45.930]just as they have shrunk in Britain, | 就像它们在英国已经萎缩一样，
[00:48.180]and the vast majority of their people will move into the city. | 绝大多数人口将迁入城市。
[00:52.230]In fact, in Britain now, only about four or 5% of people live in rural areas | 事实上，在现在的英国，只有大约4%或5%的人口居住在农村地区，
[00:58.462]and depend upon them. | 并且依赖它们。
[01:00.150]All through the developing world, the vanguard of the rural exodus | 在整个发展中国家，农村人口外流的先锋
[01:04.355]has reached the urban fringes already. | 已经到达了城市边缘。
[01:06.835]And there they huddle, | 他们在那里聚集，
[01:08.375]migrants in the favelas and barrios of Latin America, | 拉丁美洲贫民窟和棚户区的移民，
[01:12.025]in shantytowns in Africa, | 非洲的贫民窟，
[01:14.150]in those horrifying encampments one sees on the outskirts of Calcutta and Bombay. | 那些在加尔各答和孟买郊区看到的恐怖营地。
[01:19.480]We are heading towards an urban world. | 我们正在走向一个城市化的世界。
[01:22.910]This enormous increase will go ahead whatever we do. | 无论我们做什么，这种巨大的增长都将继续。
[01:26.790]And we have to remember that these new cities devour space. | 我们必须记住，这些新城市吞噬了空间。
[01:31.355]People now acquire far more goods and things. | 人们现在获得了更多的商品和物品。
[01:35.230]There is a great density of household goods. | 家庭用品的密度很高。
[01:38.210]They demand more services such as sewage and drainage. | 他们需要更多的服务，例如污水处理和排水。
[01:42.250]Above all, the car changes everything. | 最重要的是，汽车改变了一切。
[01:45.290]Rising incomes and rising populations | 收入的增长和人口的增加
[01:48.255]can make urban car density increase by something like four and 5% in a decade. | 可以在十年内使城市汽车密度增加大约4%到5%。
[01:54.230]Traffic flows rise to fill whatever scale of highways are provided for them. | 交通流量增加，以填满为它们提供的任何规模的公路。
[01:59.610]The car also has a curious ambivalence. | 汽车也有一种奇特的矛盾心理。
[02:02.995]It creates and then it destroys mobility. | 它创造了，然后又摧毁了流动性。
[02:06.230]The car tempts people further out and then gives them the appalling problem of getting back. | 汽车引诱人们走得更远，然后又让他们面临回来的可怕问题。
[02:12.000]It makes them believe that they can spend Sunday in Brighton, | 它让他们相信他们可以在布赖顿度过星期天，
[02:15.550]but makes it impossible for them to return before, say, two in the morning. | 但又让他们不可能在，比如说，凌晨两点之前回来。
[02:20.070]People go further and further away to reach open air and countryside, | 人们越走越远，去寻找开阔的空气和乡村，
[02:24.355]which continuously recedes from them. | 而这些却不断地远离他们。
[02:26.760]And just as their working weeks decline, and they begin to have more time for leisure, | 正当他们的工作周缩短，他们开始有更多闲暇时间时，
[02:31.275]they find they cannot get to the open spaces, | 他们发现自己无法到达开放空间，
[02:33.945]or the recreation, or the beaches, | 或者休闲场所，或者海滩，
[02:36.175]which they now have the time to enjoy. | 尽管他们现在有时间享受。
[02:39.025]Recently some studies were made in the behavior of mice when exposed to more than a certain degree of density, | 最近，对暴露在超过一定程度的密度、
[02:45.725]frustration, and noise. | 挫折和噪音下的老鼠行为进行了一些研究。
[02:47.750]And the mice just became deranged. | 结果老鼠变得狂躁不安。
[02:50.590]I think some sociologists wonder whether it might not be the same for men. | 我想一些社会学家在想，对人类来说会不会也是如此。
[02:55.995]This combination of very high density of population, | 这种人口、
[02:59.660]goods and services, and machines, | 商品和服务以及机器的极高密度组合，
[03:02.325]all increasing with almost brutal speed, | 所有这些都以几乎残酷的速度增长，
[03:05.040]does account for some really antisocial tendencies in modern urban growth. | 确实解释了现代城市发展中一些真正的反社会倾向。
[03:11.155]Barbara Ward | 芭芭拉·沃德
[03:13.575]The Menace of Urban Explosion | 《城市爆炸的威胁》
[03:16.235]From the listener. | 摘自《听众》杂志。